--- body ---
## Context

Maintaining separate hand-edited Claude and Codex harnesses would create immediate drift.
IDH needs a deterministic compiler from canonical sources to provider-native surfaces.
This ticket establishes the generator and proves the seam on representative content; it
does not port every skill or hook.

## Relevant files

- `scripts/gen_skills_catalog.py` — precedent for deterministic generation
- `scripts/check-skills-drift.py` — precedent for generated-output drift checks
- `CLAUDE.md` and `settings.shared.json` — Claude output targets
- `core/ARCHITECTURE.md` — ownership contract from 0801

## Actions

1. Define adapter input and output manifests with deterministic ordering.
2. Implement `scripts/build-adapters.py` with `--provider`, `--check`, and output-directory
   options; it must never overwrite canonical sources.
3. Add Claude and Codex adapter skeletons that render one instruction, one skill and one
   capability report each. The Codex skeleton must include an installable personal-plugin
   manifest rather than existing only as loose generated files.
4. Put generated artifacts under `generated/<provider>/` until their parity gates justify
   installation.
5. Document how adapters extend rather than fork canonical material.

## Test

- Add golden tests before implementation: two identical runs are byte-identical; changing
  one canonical identifier changes only its declared outputs; `--check` fails on drift.

## Verification

- [ ] Generator is deterministic and idempotent
- [ ] Unknown providers and unknown canonical identifiers fail loudly
- [ ] Claude and Codex skeletons validate in their native formats
- [ ] The generated Codex skeleton installs as a personal plugin in a clean test profile
- [ ] `make check` passes

## Invariants

- Generated files are disposable and never canonical.
- Provider adapters may add capabilities but may not redefine core semantics.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Adapter generator and two representative adapters are working
- [ ] Codex adapter skeleton is installable as a personal plugin
- [ ] Drift check is wired into the fast test gate
- [ ] Ownership of every generated path is documented
